# The info panel under the map (InfoWin, see infowin.c): the two text boxes that type out the calendar, the economy and so on, a
# letter at a time, and change by themselves. The panel's clock is stopped (its "suspended" word, 0x7ad34c) and the panel is put
# in a known state, so it changes only when the scene makes it: left clicks (the first on a box still being typed finishes it,
# a click with both done goes on to the next mode, which takes the other box), the right-click menu, and by-hand calls of the
# clock's tick (open info_tick, which lifts the stop for the call). Pokes put the game where all eight modes can be shown and
# the figures differ from zero: turn 300 (more turns than the chart is wide), a contact, the game flags the planet box needs, some
# history for the chart, a share of energy for psychic, the counts that make the graphs' title capitals, a planet state.
# What the first clicks do: the two boxes are redrawn from clean (a click on each unfinished box finishes it, then two goes on),
# leaving mode 1 in the first box and mode 2 in the second. The panel's own state is the regions iw_*.
# The typed text shows empty boxes (a character the original draws from its stack; infowin.c reproduces it).
25 load
45 click 362 734
46 poke 0x7ad34c 1            # suspended
46 poke 0x7ad320 1            # the box shown: the second
46 poke 0x7ad328 0
46 poke 0x7ad32c 0
46 poke 0x7ad330 0xffffffff   # no mode to go on from
46 poke 0x7ad334 0            # not flashing
46 poke 0x7ad348 0            # not held
46 poke 0x9a64d4 300
46 poke 0x93fab4 1
46 poke 0x9a64c0 0xd0 or
46 poke 0x96edd0 2            # the player's psychic share
46 poke 0x94b4c0 0
46 poke 0x94b4c4 0
46 poke 0x94b4c8 0
46 poke 0x9a68be 0x00640032   # the chart's history: seven factions' strength each turn, 16 bytes a turn
46 poke 0x9a68ce 0x00c80096
46 poke 0x9a68de 0x012c00fa
46 poke 0x9a68ee 0x019000c8
